---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Operation: Secure Prospective" description="Insurance producer infrastructure is SecureProspective's revenue-producing operating foundation.">
  <Nav />
  <main transition:name="page-card">
    <section class="record-hero">
      <div class="record-hero-grid shell">
        <div class="record-hero-index"><span>FILE // OPERATION</span><span>STATUS // ACTIVE</span></div>
        <div class="record-hero-copy">
          <h1>The operation is not a footnote.</h1>
          <p>
            SecureProspective serves producers now. The IMO is the revenue engine, the field environment,
            and the source of every constraint the prospective system must answer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="operating-record" class="record-section record-section--blue">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>01</strong><span>Operating record</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>Insurance producer infrastructure.</h2>
          <p>
            Independent financial professionals and small IMOs need more than product access. They need
            case intelligence, suitability discipline, carrier positioning, and an operating structure that
            can carry responsibility from first conversation through issue.
          </p>
          <table class="fact-table">
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Active producers</th><td>Approximately 8</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Annual annuity volume assisted</th><td>Approximately $18M current</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Production assisted</th><td>Approximately $110M across six years</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Operating posture</th><td>Active, revenue-producing, accountable to real cases</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section record-section--white">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>02</strong><span>What we do now</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>The work producers can use today.</h2>
          <div class="offer-grid">
            <article class="offer-item"><span>CASE // 01</span><strong>Advanced case design</strong><p>Structure complex client situations before a product is allowed to become the answer.</p></article>
            <article class="offer-item"><span>POSITION // 02</span><strong>Carrier and product positioning</strong><p>Fit the solution to the full client picture, not to a shelf or a sales target.</p></article>
            <article class="offer-item"><span>FEDERAL // 03</span><strong>Federal benefits specialty</strong><p>FERS, CSRS, TSP, FEHB, and LEO, ATC, and researcher variations.</p></article>
            <article class="offer-item"><span>CONTROL // 04</span><strong>Suitability and best interest</strong><p>Annuity suitability workflows and NY Regulation 187 discipline built into the case process.</p></article>
            <article class="offer-item"><span>FIELD // 05</span><strong>Producer development</strong><p>Training and operating support for agents who intend to build durable production.</p></article>
            <article class="offer-item"><span>SYSTEM // 06</span><strong>IMO infrastructure</strong><p>The connective operating work between producer, client, carrier, case, and obligation.</p></article>
          </div>
          <a class="action action--dark" href="mailto:secureprospective@gmail.com?subject=Producer%20infrastructure%20conversation">Start a producer conversation <span>→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section record-section--silver">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>03</strong><span>Why it matters</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>This operation gives SP+ consequences.</h2>
          <p>
            SP+ answers a problem visible inside the operation: advisors handling client PII, annuities, and
            retirement assets on general-purpose home computers. The first deliverable is an immutable Fedora
            workstation with full-disk encryption, practical application containment, and the Pi AI harness
            integrated into the daily desktop.
          </p>
          <div class="status-strip">
            <div><span>Foundation</span><strong>Immutable Fedora</strong></div>
            <div><span>Protection</span><strong>Encrypted and contained</strong></div>
            <div><span>Workflow</span><strong>Human-held AI</strong></div>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href="/the-work#sp-plus">See what is being built from it →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section record-section--ink">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>04</strong><span>Current invitation</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>If the work is insurance, start here.</h2>
          <p>Bring the case, the producer constraint, or the infrastructure problem. The first move is a direct conversation about what is actually happening.</p>
          <a class="action action--signal" href="/contact">Choose the conversation <span>→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
